Error [E0404]: `ok(...)` only fits where a fallible result is expected
  --> tests/ui/ok_outside_result.jet:2:13
    |
  2 |     val x = ok(1);
    |             ^^^^
 Why: `ok` builds the success side of `Result<T, E>`
 Fix: use it in a return type, a binding annotated with `Result<...>`, or a call that expects one
